{
    "map": {
        "description": "Derives additional  cumulative information, such as the total distance of a route or route portion  from individual segments, to prepare data for charting.",
        "in_association_table.descr": "<xdoc><p>The association table, DesigPoint_NavaidAssoc, that contains the relationships between designated points and NAVAID systems. The ATSRoute feature class&apos;s start and end designated point&apos;s <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">GFID</span> field will reference entries in this table. This table indicates whether a point is collocated with a NAVAID and helps determine the grouping of route segments.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_association_table.title": "Designated Point Navaid Association Table",
        "modified_target_atsroute_features.title": "Modified Target ATS Route Features",
        "modified_target_enroute_table.title": "Modified Target Enrouteinformation Table",
        "modified_target_routeportion_table.title": "Modified Target RoutePortion Table",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Derives additional cumulative information, such as the total distance of a route or route portion from individual segments, to prepare data for charting.</p><p>This tool identifies routes and route portions in FAA and NGA ATSRoute data.</p><p>A route collection is an ordered set of ATSRoute segments from a NAVAID to a NAVAID. For each route collection identified, an entry will be stored in the EnrouteInformation stand-alone table with the total calculated distance of each group.</p><p>A route portion collection is a subset of an en route collection containing segments from a compulsory point to a compulsory point. A route portion can also go from a NAVAID or compulsory point to a NAVAID or compulsory point. For each route portion collection identified, an entry will be stored in the RoutePortion stand-alone table.</p></xdoc>",
        "target_atsroute_features.descr": "<xdoc><p>The input feature class for the ATSRoute feature class that contains polylines. The <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Enrouteinformation_Id</span> and the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">RoutePortion_Id</span> attributes will be updated.</p></xdoc>",
        "target_atsroute_features.title": "Target ATS Route Features",
        "target_enroute_table.descr": "<xdoc><p>The table that will be updated to contain entries for the en route segments identified during processing. The <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Distance_Val</span> attribute is set to the total length of the en route segments.</p><p>The <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Distance_Val</span> attribute is updated and kept up to date on new and existing en route segments.</p></xdoc>",
        "target_enroute_table.title": "Target Enrouteinformation Table",
        "target_routeportion_table.descr": "<xdoc><p>The table that will be updated to contain entries for the route portions identified during processing. The <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">Distance_Val</span> attribute is set to the total length of the route portions&apos; segments. The route portions&apos; <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">StartPoint_Id</span> and <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">EndPoint_Id</span> attributes will also be updated to refer to the start and end point of a route portion.</p></xdoc>",
        "target_routeportion_table.title": "Target RoutePortion Table",
        "title": "Group Route Segments"
    }
}
